{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg9rigYda38CtrPYdj7N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Dq and B from the quartet bands**\n\nI used the weak-field 2×2 matrix for ⁴T₁(F) and ⁴T₁(P). The diagonal entries are −6Dq and 15B, and the off-diagonal entry is 4Dq. Energies are relative to the ⁴F term, and ⁴T₂ lies at +2Dq.\n\n- ν₁ = E(⁴T₂) − E₁ = 8 100 cm⁻¹, where E₁ is the lower eigenvalue (the ⁴T₁ ground state).\n- ν₃ = E₂ − E₁ = 2s = 19 400 cm⁻¹, so s = 9 700 cm⁻¹. Here E₂ is the upper eigenvalue (⁴T₁(P)).\n\nWith E₁ = (15B − 6Dq)/2 − s, the ν₁ condition reduces to Dq = 1.5B − 320.\n\nThe ν₃ condition is s² = (7.5B + 3Dq)² + 16Dq² = 9 700². Substituting for Dq gives 180B² − 38 400B − 91.5×10⁶ = 0.\n\nThis gives B ≈ 828 cm⁻¹ and Dq ≈ 922 cm⁻¹. These values are physically reasonable. B is about 74 % of the free-ion value for Co²⁺.\n\n**C**\n\nC can only come from the spin-forbidden band at 21 600 cm⁻¹, which I assigned as ²T₁(2). That level is not a pure term. It is a Dq-, B- and C-dependent mixture from the doublet terms ²G, ²H, ²P and ²F, so fixing C needs the full d⁷ doublet secular matrices. I did not diagonalise them by hand. Fixing C from a single mixed doublet band would also make it very sensitive to the assignment. So I do not report a value for C. Any number I gave would be a guess, such as assuming C/B ≈ 4 to 4.5.\n\n{\"Dq\": 922, \"B\": 828, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"Dq and B follow from the two spin-allowed quartet bands, but C needs full doublet-matrix diagonalisation of the mixed ²T₁(2) level, which was not done, so no value is given.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":852,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":852,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":